														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-771787">
									

<p>I so want to like this SCP. The buildup was phenominal. Mysterious photo album showing the time leading up to a seemingly motiveless murder-suicide, last two pages missing… I was like, YES, PLEASE, THIS SOUNDS TERRIFYING. But then…</p>
<p>It segues into the chronicles of an invisible dude who makes you go crazy. SO DISSAPOINTING.</p>
<p>It's like… the honeymoon was fantastic. This SCP, in the beginning, had <em>exactly</em> what I was looking for, and that first night was amazing. But a few paragraphs later, dawn broke, and I rolled over and realized that she's not as amazing as I'd drunkenly thought, and that maybe getting married in vegas to a girl I'd just met was a bad idea, and as my head pounded with hangover I raided the mini bar while wondering just how legally binding that marriage contract was, because she's not actually all that attractive and smells funny and snores really loudly and ew, is that a moustache? Oh… Oh God… that's a… but she… On the other hand, that means this wasn't a legal marriage and I'm free to slip out the back way and downvote this article for promising so much and delivering so little.</p>

							</div>

								
